# Cloudflare Pages response headers (pattern line, then indented `Name: Value` lines).
#
# Safe security headers only. We deliberately do NOT set:
#   - Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy (COEP) / Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy (COOP):
#     the signed watchlist bundle is now served SAME-ORIGIN from /bundle/origin,
#     so cross-origin isolation buys nothing; left off to avoid regressions.
#   - Content-Security-Policy (CSP): the app loads WASM, spawns web/module workers,
#     and fetches the same-origin bundle; a wrong CSP silently breaks the screen.
#     Left as a browser-validated follow-up (see docs/DEPLOY.md).
#
# HSTS: aml-filter.com is served HTTPS-only via Cloudflare Pages, so pin HTTPS for
# a year (and cover subdomains) to close the first-visit SSL-strip / downgrade
# window. This is purely additive — it constrains the TRANSPORT, never what the
# app is allowed to load — so it cannot break the WASM / worker / same-origin
# bundle screen path the way a wrong CSP/COEP would.
/*
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), microphone=(), camera=()
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains

# The ~23 MB MiniLM model (+ tokenizer/config JSONs) under /models/ is pinned by
# SHA-256 at build time (scripts/download-model.mjs) and never mutates in place,
# so a year-long immutable cache is safe. Without this rule Pages serves the
# model with `max-age=0, must-revalidate` (and no Content-Length), forcing a
# full re-download on every visit. A future weights bump must re-pin the digests
# AND move the files to a new URL path — these URLs are cached as immutable.
# Pages applies every matching block, so /models/* responses still carry the /*
# security headers above.
/models/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
